# Capturing Hover Events: Cursor and Point Pixels

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:plotly_ex, "~> 0.3"},
  {:kino, "~> 0.18"}
])
```

## Position a custom tooltip

Top-level `data["xPixel"]` and `data["yPixel"]` describe the cursor relative to
the plot. Each point's `xPixel` and `yPixel` describe its centre. The two may
differ because hover can select a nearby point. `bbox` contains the point's
bounding box when provided upstream. Missing values are `nil`.

Hover over or near a marker to compare all three measurements below.

````elixir
alias Plotly.{Figure, Scatter}
alias Plotly.Kino.PlotlyLive

output = Kino.Frame.new()

chart =
  Figure.new()
  |> Figure.add_trace(Scatter.new(
    x: [1, 2, 3, 4, 5], y: [4, 2, 6, 1, 5],
    mode: "markers", marker: %{size: 20, color: "steelblue"}
  ))
  |> Figure.update_layout(title: "Hover near a marker to compare pixels")
  |> PlotlyLive.new()

listener = spawn(fn ->
  for _ <- 1..1000 do
    receive do
      {:hover_px, %{"data" => data}} ->
        point = List.first(data["points"] || []) || %{}
        details = %{
          cursor_pixels: {data["xPixel"], data["yPixel"]},
          point_pixels: {point["xPixel"], point["yPixel"]},
          bbox: point["bbox"]
        }
        Kino.Frame.render(output, Kino.Markdown.new("```elixir\n#{inspect(details, pretty: true)}\n```"))
    after
      60_000 -> :timeout
    end
  end
end)

PlotlyLive.subscribe(chart, listener, :hover_px, :hover)
Kino.Layout.grid([chart, output])
````
